.TH MU2EDAQ\-BUILD\-ALL 1 "2026-07-23" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-build\-all \- build and install every mu2edaq\-* package for compatibility testing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh
.RB [ \-\-combined ]
.RB [ \-\-clean ]
.RI [ package\ ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh
builds and installs every package listed in the compatibility-test manifest
(\c
.BR testing/common.sh )
so that
.BR mu2edaq\-test\-all.sh
can exercise them afterwards. It is part of the
.B mu2edaq\-main
compatibility-test harness and is run from the root of the meta-repository.
.PP
Python packages each get an isolated virtual environment under
.IR .compat/venvs/<pkg> ,
built with the package's
.I requirements.txt
and, where a
.I pyproject.toml
declares one, an editable install. Sibling packages that are not published
(e.g.\&
.BR mu2edaq\-discovery )
are installed into a dependent package's venv from the local checkout first.
CMake-based packages are configured and built under
.IR .compat/build/<pkg> .
.PP
The script keeps going after a failure in one package so that a single run
reports the status of the whole suite, and exits non-zero if any package
failed.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.RI [ package\ ... ]
Build only the named package(s) instead of the full manifest. Unknown names
are skipped with a warning.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-combined
After building each package individually, additionally install every
package's
.I requirements.txt
into one shared venv
.RI ( .compat/venvs/_combined )
and run
.B pip check
against it. This surfaces cross-package dependency conflicts that per-package
venvs cannot reveal.
.TP
.B \-\-clean
Remove
.I .compat/venvs
and
.I .compat/build
before building, forcing every venv and CMake build directory to be recreated
from scratch.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B .compat/status/build.tsv
One row per build step per package:
.IR pkg ", " step ", " "PASS/FAIL/SKIP" ", " logfile ", " timestamp .
Reset at the start of every run.
.TP
.B .compat/logs/build/
Full command output for every step, one log file per package/step.
.TP
.B .compat/venvs/<pkg>/
Per-package Python virtual environment (Python packages only).
.TP
.B .compat/build/<pkg>[\-\-<subdir>]/
Per-package CMake build directory (CMake packages only; the
.RI \-\- <subdir>
suffix is used for packages whose CMake project lives in a subdirectory,
e.g.\&
.IR cpp/ ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_PYTHON
Interpreter used to create venvs. Default:
.BR python3 .
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_COMPAT_DIR
Root directory for all harness artifacts. Default:
.IR <repo\-root>/.compat .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every requested package built successfully.
.TP
.B non-zero
At least one package failed to build; the failing package names are printed
and recorded in
.BR build.tsv .
.SH EXAMPLES
Build and install everything:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh
.EE
Build everything and also check for cross-package pip conflicts:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh \-\-combined
.EE
Wipe all venvs/builds and start over:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh \-\-clean
.EE
Build just one package:
.EX
    ./mu2edaq\-build\-all.sh mu2edaq\-fts
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-test\-all (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-setup\-env (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-main
.UE
